title: Chapter1_Overworld
---
// TODO: Use Overworld_Ch1 as prefix for nodes. Change title of this file too.
// See the global state- CURRENT_SCENE is where we get the prefix. We should be using node names.
// When the Dialogue Control switches to new scenes, it should "reload" the yarn script we're loading in
<<declare $name = "Merk">>
<<declare $checked_for_permit = false>>
<<declare $talked_to_old_man = false>>
<<declare $talked_to_sad_guard = false>>
===

// Just a chill dude leaning back on the bridge, potentially with a bag of some sort
// Pretty hooded figure, something mysterious. Can come back much later in the game
// Should have some "business"- smoking is the right vibe, but not sure I want to do that
title: Overworld_Bystander
---
Bystander: Hey, $name, glad to see you're making it back before the Closing tonight. You've been cutting it close!
-> So much to do, need to make use of the hours
-> It's easy to lose track of time out here
Bystander: Can't argue with that. I'll be riding through the night tonight. Some weird ask to gather some Night Pheasants...
Bystander: Good luck getting in then!
===

// This is someone that appears to be some sort of armored mercenary
// She's got a slight attitude, and the other guy is scrambling to get her payment
title: Overworld_Mercenary
---
Miranda: Hey, if it ain't Tea Guy. You end up running into those grunts at the river, too?
-> Nope, must have missed them!
-> Yea, I ended up skirting around them.
Miranda: Well, really a pain in my ass. But hey, that's why they hire me...
Miranda: Anyway, I'll come in a bit for my minty regular. Just waiting on my coin.
Sketchy Farmer: Uh, yes, uhh, it's in here somewhere...
===

// This is a sketchy farmer that's been escorted here by the mercenary
// He's a farmer, a cart, but something is a little sketchy
// TODO: If you talk to the mercenary first, say she's paid and something else. Those vars can just exist within here.
title: Overworld_SketchyFarmer
---
Sketchy Farmer: Once I pay her, I'm good to go. I got my permit, got the vials, I'll just need to spread it...
Sketchy Farmer: Heh? What are you eavesdropping in on?
===

title: Overworld_CitadelGuard
---
// I'm structuring booleans such that the first event is what we check first
// TODO: Branching dialogue options, maybe?
<<if $checked_for_permit == false && $talked_to_old_man == false && $talked_to_sad_guard == false>>
  Citadel Guard: Permit, please...
    -> Uhhhh...
  Citadel Guard: *sigh* Come on, $name, you know the drill. I can't let you in, sorry.
  <<set $checked_for_permit to true>>
<<elseif $checked_for_permit == true && $talked_to_old_man == false && $talked_to_sad_guard == false>>
  // TODO: Shuffle responses or something
  Citadel Guard: Still no permit? No entry. I don't make the rules
    -> Come on, you've seen me come in!
  Citadel Guard: I don't make the rules, and I'd rather not put my job on the line
<<elseif $talked_to_sad_guard == true>>
  Citadel Guard: I'm on my break, go bother Andy
<<else>> // if talked_to_old_man is true
  Citadel Guard: Look, if you don't have a permit to get in, I can't let you in. That's just my jo-
  <<trigger_animation "old_man_approaches_at_gate">>
<<endif>>
===

title: Overworld_OldMan
---
Old Man: Ah, $name, I'm so lucky to have you!
  -> I didn't get much today...
  -> I was a little carried away on my own task...
Old Man: Bah, that's alright. It's a quiet night and I'm sure we've got plenty to get by with
Old Man: I just need to tie these together, then I'll meet you up at the gate!
<<set $talked_to_old_man to true>>
===

title: Overworld_SadGuard
---
// TODO: I think I should set a flag that's more like "cheered_up_sad_guard"
// But right now, you can only talk to one of them anyway so it works
<<if $talked_to_sad_guard == false>>
  You approach Andy, a sad looking guard looking wistfully looks off into the distance, in an old looking uniform.
  Sad Guard: *sigh*
    -> Watcha eating?
    -> You appear lost in thought...
  Sad Guard: Ah, it's nothing... just...
  Sad Guard: Today, we've turned away the most people today in a while, and it hurts every time.
  Sad Guard: We were supposed to be the peace! The safe haven! We're built off of visitors and yet... we have to allow only those with proper permits?
    -> At the end of the day, you're just doing your job
    -> Yea that sucks, at least your heart's in the right place
  Happy Guard: I suppose there's that. Though maybe I can figure something out...
  Happy Guard: Anyway, I guess that's my break.
  <<set $talked_to_sad_guard to true>>
  <<trigger_animation "sad_guard_replaces_other_guard">>
<<else>>
  Happy Guard: Ah, hey! Look you seem well intentioned but I can't let you in.
  Happy Guard: Uh, though, some permits do allow a second party, so...
  <<trigger_animation "old_man_approaches_at_gate">>
<<endif>>

===

// Every node will need the "scene" prefix pretty much
title: Overworld_OldManCitadelEnter
---
<<if $talked_to_old_man == true>>
Old Man: Ah, there you are young fellow! I was wondering where my hired help had gone off to
Old Man: Good day sir, you can see my open second designation for helpers on the bottom right.
Citadel Guard: Hmm... looks good then, carry on.
Citadel Guard: Make sure to stick with your employer next time.
<<elseif $talked_to_sad_guard == true>>
Old Man: If you'd be willing to help an old man carry some boxes, I have a secondary designation here!
Old Man: One of my strings broke...
// He doesn't even look at the permit
Sad Guard: That works for me! Carry on- oh! and thanks for the chat. Maybe this kind of thing will help out
<<endif>>
===
